{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>חשן משפט.</b> That it atones for corruption of justice. Another interpretation: משפט — that makes His words and His guarantee true, דריש\"נטנט בְּלַעַז; for משפט serves three meanings — the arguments of the litigants, the conclusion of the case, and the penalty of the case — whether the penalty of death, whether the penalty of lashes, whether the penalty of money. And here it serves the sense of clarification of matters, that He explains and makes clear His words." "<b>כמעשה אפד.</b> Work of a weaver, and of five kinds."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "the la'az דריש\"נטנט is Old French dreit entent or droiturentente, 'right/true understanding'; the sense turns on reading משפט as ברור דברים."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:11.931624474Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}